# Unowned libraries

Owned related libraries (submodules this fleet maintains): rule `repository-boundaries`.

**CONSTRAINT:** MUST NOT suggest editing, forking, opening an upstream PR on, or pinning a patched fork of a library this workspace does not own. MUST recommend a workaround in owned code instead.

Before a reply or plan names a library change as the next step, complete this gate in working memory:

```text
Candidate: [module or repo name]
Owned origin: YES: [quote a workspace git remote or go.mod replace path] / NO
User asked to change that library: YES: [quote] / NO
Decision: MAY edit in that owning repo | MUST NOT suggest changing | refuse and give owned workaround
```

If Owned origin is NO and the user did not ask to change that library: Decision is MUST NOT suggest changing.
If Owned origin is NO and the user asked to change that library: Decision is refuse and give owned workaround.
If Owned origin is YES: Decision is MAY edit in that owning repo (then follow repository-boundaries).

- MUST: treat a library as owned only when a workspace checkout has that origin remote, or `go.mod` replace points at such a checkout
- MUST: when the library is unowned, recommend an owned-side change (adapter, config, provider, or skip the path)
- MUST NOT: recommend an upstream PR, a fork, a patched-version pin, edits under the module cache, or edits under `tmp/<library-name>`
- MAY: clone unowned source into `tmp/<library-name>` to read. MUST NOT modify or commit that clone
- MAY: name the unowned library as the mechanism of a bug

Enforcement: before send, if the draft names a library change, confirm the gate ran and that Owned origin YES quotes a remote or replace path
Violation: STOP, drop the unowned-library change, rewrite the next step as owned code or config

CORRECT:
```text
llm-go rejects trailing SSE
→ Owned origin NO (require github.com/XiaoConstantine/llm-go; no workspace remote)
→ Recommend a strop adapter or a provider switch in operator config
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
llm-go rejects trailing SSE
→ Pin llm-go v0.3.7 or open an upstream PR
```

CORRECT:
```text
User: patch the strop heartbeat
→ Owned origin YES: origin git@github.com:behaviorengineering/strop.git
→ Edit in the strop checkout
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
User: patch XiaoConstantine/llm-go
→ Edit tmp/llm-go or open an upstream PR
```
